CHANGELOG.md	- A window onto a macOS VM run opens on an unlocked Mac again. rc.12 refused every open with `mac_window_lock_unknown`, because macOS leaves out the session's screen-lock key while the screen is unlocked. A missing key now reads as unlocked; a lock key that reads true, or a lock notification, still refuses and closes an open window.	reworded in the v0.10.0-rc.13 release: the same fix bullet with its real-Mac status added
CHANGELOG.md	- On an interactive macOS VM run (`wardyn run --machine-kind macos_vm --experience interactive --window`, or `desktop_window: "at_start"`), the window now opens once the run's preparation finishes. Before, it was asked for while preparation was still running, refused as preparing, and never asked again.	reworded in the v0.10.0-rc.13 release: the same fix bullet with its real-Mac status added
